MODEL AND DATA NOTICE
---------------------
The model release this demo serves lives in the same repository, on `main`, and
carries its own NOTICE. It is a factual forecasting research artifact derived
from credentialed MIMIC-IV and eICU data. It contains no row-level patient
records, but the trained weights and fitted target heads must not be made public
or shared with anyone who is not authorized under the applicable PhysioNet data
use agreements. A public release of derived models would have to be distributed
through PhysioNet under the same agreement as the source data.

The artifact is not a medical device, is not clinically validated, and must not
be used to make treatment decisions. It supports factual forecasting only; every
output sets `causal_claim_allowed` to `false`.

THIRD-PARTY ASSETS
------------------
The anatomical artwork under `frontend/assets/anatomy-motion/` is third-party
work under its own terms, and those terms are not affected by anything above.
Each asset's licence, source and modifications are recorded per asset — never
per collection — in:

    frontend/assets/anatomy-motion/PROVENANCE.json    the record of record
    frontend/assets/anatomy-motion/ATTRIBUTION.md     the human-readable summary
    frontend/assets/anatomy-motion/organs/SOURCES.json  per organ illustration

In outline: the body figure is public domain (LadyofHats / Mariana Ruiz
Villarreal, via Wikimedia Commons); the organ illustrations are public domain
(NIH BioArt Source, NIAID Visual & Medical Arts, credited to Ryan Kissinger,
courtesy of NIAID); the anterior brain and the placement manifest were authored
for this project. A recommended credit line is kept wherever a source asks for
one, including where the licence does not compel it.

Read PROVENANCE.json before adding, replacing or removing anything in that
directory.
